WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:01.925
PRIYANKA VERGADIA:
Today, we're talking

00:00:01.925 --> 00:00:04.860
about code samples, security,
and a different kind

00:00:04.860 --> 00:00:05.940
of chatbot.

00:00:05.940 --> 00:00:09.090
I am Priyanka, and welcome to
"This Week in Cloud," where

00:00:09.090 --> 00:00:12.000
we serve you the
lowest latency news.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:15.810
For the first time ever,
cloud.google.com's code samples

00:00:15.810 --> 00:00:18.850
can be searched from
a single location.

00:00:18.850 --> 00:00:23.160
So far, the search page
includes 8,600 code samples

00:00:23.160 --> 00:00:25.440
across seven
programming languages

00:00:25.440 --> 00:00:29.470
with language, product, and
keyword filters available.

00:00:29.470 --> 00:00:32.100
Check out the blog post
to learn more or head over

00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:37.320
to
cloud.google.com/docs/samples.

00:00:37.320 --> 00:00:41.880
Join us for our first Google
Cloud Security Talks of 2021--

00:00:41.880 --> 00:00:45.060
a live online event
on March 3, where

00:00:45.060 --> 00:00:48.630
we will help you navigate
the latest in cloud security.

00:00:48.630 --> 00:00:52.620
Reserve your virtual seat now
to hear experts discuss topics

00:00:52.620 --> 00:00:55.260
like risk management,
information governance

00:00:55.260 --> 00:00:59.040
in Google Workspace, machine
learning to better protect

00:00:59.040 --> 00:01:02.170
networks, the future of
confidential computing,

00:01:02.170 --> 00:01:03.720
and more.

00:01:03.720 --> 00:01:06.030
Getting the job
you want requires

00:01:06.030 --> 00:01:08.820
you to stand out to
potential employers,

00:01:08.820 --> 00:01:11.160
especially in the
current job market.

00:01:11.160 --> 00:01:13.500
Recently, one of our
customer engineers

00:01:13.500 --> 00:01:17.100
did just that by building
a conversational chatbot

00:01:17.100 --> 00:01:19.500
on Google Cloud that
answers questions

00:01:19.500 --> 00:01:21.390
about professional experience.

00:01:21.390 --> 00:01:23.280
Plus some surprises.

00:01:23.280 --> 00:01:27.390
Check out a new way to stand
out and learn more on the blog.

00:01:27.390 --> 00:01:30.310
If you want to stop those
clever phishing attacks,

00:01:30.310 --> 00:01:31.710
use security keys.

00:01:31.710 --> 00:01:34.110
A security key is
a physical device

00:01:34.110 --> 00:01:37.260
that works alongside your
user name and password

00:01:37.260 --> 00:01:40.770
to verify your identity
to a site or an app.

00:01:40.770 --> 00:01:43.110
They produce stronger
login protection

00:01:43.110 --> 00:01:45.810
than an authenticator
app or SMS code.

00:01:45.810 --> 00:01:49.450
And the same device can
be used for many services.

00:01:49.450 --> 00:01:51.180
So you don't need
to carry around

00:01:51.180 --> 00:01:53.790
a necklace of dongles or fobs.

00:01:53.790 --> 00:01:57.900
In this issue of GCP Comics,
we are covering exactly that.

00:01:57.900 --> 00:02:00.480
Check it out for more.

00:02:00.480 --> 00:02:02.910
If you want to read more
about these announcements

00:02:02.910 --> 00:02:05.470
or see a full list,
check out the link.

00:02:05.470 --> 00:02:09.070
Any thoughts or ideas, leave
us a comment or tweet us.

00:02:09.070 --> 00:02:11.870
We'll see you in the Cloud.

